 person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lorimer</surname><given-names>JW</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Is prophylactic resection valid as an indication for elective surgery in diverticular disease?</article-title><source>Can J Surg</source><year>1997</year><volume>40</volume><fpage>445</fpage><lpage>448</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Lorimer JW (1997) Is prophylactic resection valid as an indication for elective surgery in diverticular disease? Can J Surg 40:445&#x02013;448 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9416254</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR10"><label>10.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Leigh</surname><given-names>JE</given-names></name><name><surname>Judd</surname><given-names>ES</given-names></name><name><surname>Waugh</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Diverticulitis of the colon. Recurrence after apparently adequate segmental resection</article-title><source>Am J Surg</source><year>1962</year><volume>103</volume><fpage>51</fpage><lpage>54</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/0002-9610(62)90012-0</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Leigh JE, Judd ES, Waugh JM (1962) Diverticulitis of the colon. Recurrence after apparently adequate segmental resection. Am J Surg 103:51&#x02013;54 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14463838</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR11"><label>11.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Benn</surname><given-names>PL</given-names></name><name><surname>Wolff</surname><given-names>BG</given-names></name><name><surname>Ilstrup</surname><given-names>DM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Level of anastomosis and recurrent colonic diverticulitis</article-title><source>Am J Surg</source><year>1986</year><volume>151</volume><fpage>269</fpage><lpage>271</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1